# Store and check out every file byte-for-byte, with no line-ending conversion.
#
# The A1 repository was checked out on Windows with core.autocrlf=true, so the
# working tree held CRLF copies of LF files. That made DVC hash different bytes
# on Windows and Linux, and made a packaged Windows tree show ~145 "modified"
# files on Linux. Some pipeline outputs are CRLF on purpose (Python's csv module
# writes \r\n), so files are not normalised either way: what is committed is
# exactly what every platform checks out and what DVC hashes.
#
# "-text" alone would also make git treat every file as binary in diffs and
# merges, so diff and merge are switched back on, except for real binaries.
* -text diff merge

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.pdf binary
*.docx binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.mp4 binary
*.sqlite3 binary
*.db binary
*.pyc binary
